  "term": "Stevens–Johnson syndrome",
  "definition": "Stevens–Johnson syndrome is a disorder in which the outer skin layer separates from the deeper skin layer over less than 10% of the body. It is thought to be a hypersensitivity reaction that affects both the skin and the mucous membranes.",
